# Build-context exclusions for the proof images built FROM this directory
# (Dockerfile.oracle-pack / Dockerfile.probe-pack / Dockerfile.as /
# Dockerfile.agentos-proof all take $PROOF_DIR as their context).
#
# Without this file the interpreter caches below are COPY'd into the proof
# images — stale bytecode compiled from a DIFFERENT source revision than the
# one the image's provenance label names. That is a provenance defect, not a
# size one: an image labelled with commit X must not carry .pyc compiled from
# commit W. Python is told not to write bytecode at runtime
# (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE), so nothing in the image needs these.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Never let a per-run private artefact reach a build context. These are minted
# into a mktemp dir, not here, so this is belt-and-braces against a future
# change that stages them in-tree: keys, certs, realm credentials, tokens.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
realm-credentials.env
realm-subjects.env
*-tokens.json

# Local tool caches / editor droppings.
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
